```
id: SPL-019
name: DNS tunneling indicators
description: A host sends many unique, long queries to a single parent domain.
platform: Splunk
mitre_tactic: Command and Control
mitre_technique: T1071.004 Application Layer Protocol: DNS
severity: Medium
data_source: index=dns
false_positives: Content delivery and anti-malware lookups that use long encoded labels.
tuning: Exclude known security-vendor and CDN domains via lookup.
test_method: Send a series of long random-label queries to a lab domain.
owner: <OWNER>
status: Draft
last_review: 2026-11-19
```
index=dns earliest=-1h
| eval qlen=len(query)
| eval parts=split(query,".")
| eval parent=mvindex(parts,-2).".".mvindex(parts,-1)
| stats count dc(query) AS unique_queries avg(qlen) AS avg_len BY src, parent
| where unique_queries>=200 AND avg_len>=40
| sort - unique_queries
